# Level one

Add a first browse level only when the collection is large enough to need one, and choose broad, familiar subjects. An extra level costs a click, so it must save more effort than it spends. For example, a “Lighting” page can introduce scenes, bulbs and schedules. A small setup should keep its task links on one page. The hierarchy itself is described in [Mainstream browse](../mainstream-browse.html).

## When to use it

Use it when a documentation or help collection is large enough to need it. Add a one-sentence description where a name alone is ambiguous.

## Structure and behaviour

Use a clear heading, a concise introduction and a plain list of subtopics. Curated links may come first when you can show why they matter. Do not call them “Most viewed” without evidence. Keep topic links separate from immediate device actions.

## Home Assistant boundary

This reference collects no analytics and does not change Home Assistant areas. A first-level page must not become an extra compulsory click before common tasks. Popularity ranking is not a household requirement.

